= The Relief Package

The economy is in free fall. Congress is negotiating a historic relief bill: direct payments, expanded unemployment insurance, and loans to business. How big should it be?

- @relief_huge: Go big
- @relief_mid: A targeted package
- @relief_small: Hold the line on spending

@relief_huge
on-arrival: stimulus_level += 2; economic_growth += 2.5; unemployed -= 0.8; budget -= 2; working_dem += 3*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent -= 3; inflation += 0.3

We back the largest relief effort in history. The recovery will be faster, and perhaps hotter.

@relief_mid
on-arrival: stimulus_level += 1; economic_growth += 1.5; unemployed -= 0.4; budget -= 1; moderate_strength += 2

A targeted package passes, with bipartisan support.

@relief_small
on-arrival: economic_growth -= 0.5; unemployed += 0.4; budget += 1; progressive_dissent += 6; working_dem -= 2*(1-dissent); biz_relation += 2

We refuse to be spenders. Families face a long recovery.
